<title>MEXICO: Sanluis 1996 net grows 106 pct.</title>
<headline>Sanluis 1996 net grows 106 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sanluis Corp, the autopart and mining firm, reported a 106 percent rise in net profits in 1996 to 421 million pesos, which lifted earnings per CPO to 5.30 pesos from 2.56 pesos in 1995.</p>
<p>In a statement, it said net sales in 1996 reached 1.979 billion pesos, a 13 percent rise from the year before. In dollar terms, revenues rose 29 percent over the same period to $236 million, because the exchange rate slipped at a lower rate than inflation last year.</p>
<p>Operating earnings before tax, depreciation and interest, was up 18 percent last year to $65 million, it added.</p>
<p>Among its activities, the company mines gold and silver.</p>
<p>((--Henry Tricks, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9560))</p>
